  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q2_Cabling
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: What makes a cable a cross-over cable?
  choices:
  - Both ends are wired to T568A
  - One end is T568A and the other end is T568B
  - The conductors are crossed inside the jacket
  - Only four of the eight conductors are used
  correctChoiceIndex: 1
  points: 10
  explanation: Using a different standard at each end swaps the transmit and receive
    pairs, so two like devices can talk directly. A straight-through cable uses the
    same standard at both ends.
